      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Neoadjuvant chemotherapy(NAC)is thought to be effective to improve the outcomes in patients with adenocarcinoma of the esophago-gastric junction(AEG). We encountered 3 patients who were confirmed as having a pathological complete response following gastrectomy after NAC. The first patient had Siewert type II and clinical Stage III AEG, the second patient had Siewert type I and clinical Stage III AEG, while the third had Siewert type II and clinical Stage II AEG. Two patients received NAC with 2 courses of S-1 plus cisplatin, while the third patient received 2 courses of docetaxel, S-1, and cisplatin. All of the patients were treated with D2 gastrectomy after the NAC, and remain alive at more than 40 months after initial chemotherapy treatment without recurrence. We report the details of these 3 cases and review the literature."},
